From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Register int64 scalar operator overloads before double

bind_in_place_binary_scalars/bind_binary_scalars/bind_reverse_binary_scalars/
bind_comparison_scalars each register two overloads of the same Python
method name (__add__, __iadd__, __eq__, ...) onto Variable/DataArray/
Dataset: one for a C++ double right-hand side, one for int64_t. pybind11
tries overloads in registration order and takes the first whose argument
converts, and these always registered the double overload first.

Under pybind11 2.x that didn't matter: a plain Python int failed the
double overload's (stricter, in that version) conversion check and fell
through to int64_t. pybind11 3.x loosened float's conversion check to
accept int (pybind/pybind11#5879, "float now accepts int" for PEP 484
compatibility), so the double overload now matches first and every
scalar operation silently promotes int-valued results to float64
throughout scipp's Python layer (copy, add_equals, concat, ...).

Register int64_t first so the exact-type overload still wins for a
Python int under either pybind11 generation; double remains available
for everything else (floats, numpy float scalars, etc.) exactly as
before. This only reorders registration - none of the operators'
actual implementations change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 lib/python/bind_operators.h | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/python/bind_operators.h b/lib/python/bind_operators.h
index d444aab..7848439 100644
--- a/lib/python/bind_operators.h
+++ b/lib/python/bind_operators.h
@@ -351,26 +351,26 @@ static void bind_comparison(pybind11::class_<T, Ignored...> &c) {

 template <class T, class... Ignored>
 void bind_in_place_binary_scalars(pybind11::class_<T, Ignored...> &c) {
-  OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::in_place_binary<double>(c);
   OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::in_place_binary<int64_t>(c);
+  OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::in_place_binary<double>(c);
 }

 template <class T, class... Ignored>
 void bind_binary_scalars(pybind11::class_<T, Ignored...> &c) {
-  OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::binary<double>(c);
   OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::binary<int64_t>(c);
+  OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::binary<double>(c);
 }

 template <class T, class... Ignored>
 static void bind_reverse_binary_scalars(pybind11::class_<T, Ignored...> &c) {
-  OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::reverse_binary<double>(c);
   OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::reverse_binary<int64_t>(c);
+  OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::reverse_binary<double>(c);
 }

 template <class T, class... Ignored>
 void bind_comparison_scalars(pybind11::class_<T, Ignored...> &c) {
-  OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::comparison<double>(c);
   OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::comparison<int64_t>(c);
+  OpBinder<ScalarToVariable>::comparison<double>(c);
 }

 template <class T, class... Ignored>
